  "details": "When using auto-send on the chatbox, messages persist even when the message is fully deleted.\n\nI believe this behaviour is strange because when using auto-type, you're expecting what's inside the chatbox to mirror what's on top of your head at all times. This is likely a bug when referring to deleting the message, but I've marked this as a feature request because I also believe that this should be the case when closing the chatbox.\n\nWhen the chatbox is closed, the message inside is erased, therefore it should be removed from your head. The message not getting deleted when the chatbox is closed creates a dissonance between what the player is able to intuitively know about what's on top of their head.\n\n**Proposed behaviour:**\n\n- Closing the chatbox with a message inside and auto-send enabled makes the message disappear after a few seconds, regardless of chatbox duration settings.\n\n- Erasing the text inside the chatbox with auto-send enabled makes the message disappear instantly.\n\n- Manually hitting \"Send\" with auto-send enabled ignores these behaviours and behaves identically to a manually-sent message. (Respects \"chatbox duration\" setting.)",
